. * IMPORTANT NOTE: THINKING ABOUT ADDING IN AGE AS A CONTROL???? 
. gen age_days = int_date - mdy(bmonth, bday, byear)
(16,838 missing values generated)

. gen age_months_exact = age_days / 30.4375
(16,838 missing values generated)

. * CHANGED: Same rule as 2002 and 2005, for ALL interviews. Some Book S birth 
> dates are wrong, or the Book C date is long after the measurement (2011-2013 
> interviews: 75% of ages disagree in 2013). If the computed age disagrees with
>  the age reported in Book S (sa03) by more than about a year, set age_days to
>  missing so the child gets no z-score
. gen int int_year = year(int_date)
(3,517 missing values generated)

. replace age_days = . if !missing(age, age_days) & !inrange(age_days/365.25 - 
> age, -0.5, 1.5)
(2,884 real changes made, 2,884 to missing)

. 
. * The check above uses the Book C date because the Book S age sa03 is the ros
> ter age from the Book C visit for most of 2009 children. Children who pass ge
> t their age at the Book S measurement date, and int_date becomes that date, o
> r the Book C date if there is none, so the interview month FE and the Novembe
> r 2009 cutoff use it too
. replace age_days = meas_date - mdy(bmonth, bday, byear) if !missing(age_days,
>  meas_date)
(27,218 real changes made)

. replace int_date = meas_date if !missing(meas_date)
(38,086 real changes made)

. drop meas_date

. replace age_months_exact = age_days / 30.4375
(30,102 real changes made, 2,884 to missing)

