.     * This file also creates prevelance tables in the code provided from git 
> and erases the data _zlen, _zwei, and _zbmi, so we just need to reload them 
.         use "$who_output_dir/mxfls2009_u5_z_rc.dta", clear
(ENNVIH-3 Libro s_sa)

.     * The original ado computes flags but it doesn't implement the flags and 
> remove implausible z-scores, here we implement it
.     gen haz = _zlen if _flen == 0
(1,237 missing values generated)

.     gen waz = _zwei if _fwei == 0
(19 missing values generated)

.     gen bmiz = _zbmi if _fbmi == 0
(1,258 missing values generated)

.         * Implement a check to count how many got flagged/excluded as out-of-
> range
.     count if _flen == 1
  6

.     di "u5: `r(N)' HAZ obs flagged out of range (<-6 or >6)"
u5: 6 HAZ obs flagged out of range (<-6 or >6)

.     count if _fwei == 1
  7

.     di "u5: `r(N)' WAZ obs flagged out of range (<-6 or >5)"
u5: 7 WAZ obs flagged out of range (<-6 or >5)

.     count if _fbmi == 1
  15

.     di "u5: `r(N)' BMIZ obs flagged out of range (<-5 or >5)"
u5: 15 BMIZ obs flagged out of range (<-5 or >5)

.     keep folio ls haz waz bmiz

.     save `z_u5'
