. ** TESTING ****
. ***************
. * Maternal/Household Child Mortality (Book 4, Reproductive Health)
. * NOTE: iv_res is a mother-level LIFETIME cumulative measure (every child she
> 's ever borne, as of the 2009 interview) -- not a birth-year-specific outcome
>  like. We collapse it to household level
. *use "$path/hh09dta_b4/iv_res.dta", clear
. *keep folio ls res03 res04 res07 res08 res10 res11 res13
. *rename res10 sons_died
. *rename res11 daughters_died
. *rename res13 stillbirths
. * children_ever_born_alive = living with her (res03/04) + alive elsewhere (re
> s07/08)
. *                            + died after being born alive (sons_died/daughte
> rs_died)
. *gen children_ever_born_alive = res03 + res04 + res07 + res08 + sons_died + d
> aughters_died
. *gen children_died = sons_died + daughters_died
. *tempfile temp_mortality
. *save `temp_mortality'
. * Sum numerator and denominator ACROSS all mothers in the household before
. * dividing -- summing first avoids a "ratio of ratios" mistake if a household
. * has more than one woman with a birth history.
. *collapse (sum) children_ever_born_alive children_died stillbirths, by(folio)
. *gen child_mortality_rate = 100 * children_died / children_ever_born_alive if
>  children_ever_born_alive > 0
. *label variable child_mortality_rate "HH lifetime child deaths per 100 live b
> irths (mothers' birth histories, cumulative to 2009)"
. *tempfile temp_mortality_hh
. *save `temp_mortality_hh'
