. * We keep the Book C state aka edo together with mpio so each municipality si
> ts inside its own state, and build the 5 digit INEGI key cvegeo = 2 digit sta
> te + 3 digit municipality.
. * NOTE: 21 Book C cover rows have no state or municipality, all with book int
> erview result rel = 21. None of these households has a measured child, so we 
> leave them missing 
. preserve

.     use "$path/hh09dta_bc/c_portad.dta", clear
(LIBRO C portad MxFLS 2009)

.     keep folio ent mpio loc

.         * It was checked for the majority that 35 households coded 15-011 in 
> 2009 come from households that were in 15-110 in 2002 and 2005. Contrary to t
> he mg08a survey that says these households didn't move. That accounts for mos
> t of them but a couple are assumed, but this is a legit assumption. So 011 is
>  a typo for 110, digits reversed.
.     replace mpio = 110 if ent == 15 & mpio == 11
(35 real changes made)

.     * We checked this. This is likely coded incorrectly because same locality
> , same January 2010 field trip, and the MG08a answers. Matches the other surv
> ey waves
.     replace mpio = 102 if ent == 16 & mpio == 10 & loc == 15
(14 real changes made)

.     gen str5 cvegeo = string(ent, "%02.0f") + string(mpio, "%03.0f") if !miss
> ing(ent, mpio)
(21 missing values generated)

