. 
. * This code works. The letters being skipped 7,8 denote the wave and member t
> ype. To match the 10 format of the other waves this code does so
. capture confirm string variable pid_link

. if _rc tostring pid_link, replace format(%012.0f)

. gen wave = 2009

. 
. * We basically grab the digits 1-6, 9-12 for individuals in waves 1 and 2. Bu
> t if this is a new individual only in this wave we keep the whole thing and t
> hey get a new pid_link_canonical so they don't mistakenly try to match with a
>  previous wave.  
. gen pid_link_canonical = cond(substr(pid_link,7,1) == "C", "09_" + pid_link, 
> substr(pid_link,1,6) + substr(pid_link,9,2) + substr(pid_link,11,2))
(5,832 missing values generated)

